questions.answer:
The function `fact(n)` has a time complexity of $O(n)$, as it makes $n$ recursive calls.

**Modified algorithm**

```c
int sumfact(int n) {
    if (n == 1) return 1;
    if (n == 0) return 1;
    else {
        int temp = fact(n - 1) * n;    // n!
        return temp + sumfact(n - 1);
    }
}
```

**Bottom-up (different way)**

```c
int sumfactDP(int n) {
    int DP[n + 1];
    DP[0] = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
        DP[i] = i * DP[i - 1];
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
        sum += DP[i];
    return sum;
}
```

**Overlapping subproblems:** in the modified recursive algorithm, the factorials of all previous terms have to be recomputed for each term of the series. This is avoided using DP.

**Time complexity:**

- old (recursive): each of the $n$ calls computes a factorial in $O(n)$, so $O(n^2)$
- new (bottom-up DP): $O(n)$

Here the m array is the DP table of the MCM algorithm. The code below uses 0-based indexing; the hand calculation uses 1-based indexing.

```c
int MCMBU(int arr[], int n) {
    int dp[n][n];
    for (int slide = 1; slide < n; slide++) {
        for (int si = 0; si < n - slide; si++) {
            int ei = si + slide;
            if (si + 1 == ei) dp[si][ei] = 0;
            else {
                int min = INT_MAX;
                for (int k = si + 1; k < ei; k++) {
                    int fp = dp[si][k];
                    int sp = dp[k][ei];
                    int sw = arr[si] * arr[k] * arr[ei];
                    int total = fp + sp + sw;
                    if (total < min) min = total;
                }
                dp[si][ei] = min;
            }
        }
    }
    return dp[0][n - 1];
}
```

**Calculation** ($p_0 = 3$, $p_1 = 1$, $p_2 = 2$, $p_3 = 1$):

- $m(1,1) = m(2,2) = m(3,3) = 0$
- $m(1,2) = p_0 p_1 p_2 = 6$
- $m(2,3) = p_1 p_2 p_3 = 2$
- $m(1,3) = \min\{ m(1,1) + m(2,3) + p_0 p_1 p_3,\ m(1,2) + m(3,3) + p_0 p_2 p_3 \} = \min\{0 + 2 + 3,\ 6 + 0 + 6\} = 5$

